{"id":"rs_tmp_i2c96he35d","type":"reasoning","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"reasoning_text","text":"I'm reconsidering whether writing to the vault counts as a prohibited action under plan mode—even though it's outside the working tree, it's still a state-changing write, and the guard rejects any such writes except local:// session artifacts. So I shouldn't perform the vault write while in plan mode.

Instead, I'll explain this limitation, present the drafted content, and offer to write it once plan mode is off. Since local:// writes are explicitly allowed, I can save the draft there now as local://knowledge-home-decision.md, keeping it ready for later. The draft itself should stay concise and grounded: ProjectRecord already holds omp-ui-owned per-project state like browserClock and reviewRoster (per issue #738/ADR-0047), .omp/config.yml belongs to omp, and vault paths are machine-local so they shouldn't be committed to repo config—consistent with how the prototype handles vault ids and defaultVaultId.

"}],"summary":[],"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ","format":"anthropic-claude-v1"}
